Cachyborne's optional contact-shadow/PCSS compute shader is adapted from the
GPL-2.0-or-later source file contact_shadow.comp in Lantern Engine by Awaken
(https://github.com/Awakenchan/LanternEngine), revision e6b943dd. The host integration
and validation are changed for Cachyborne's renderer. This is not an official
Lantern Engine release; Lantern's name, logos and branding are not used for this port.

GX barrier assistance and keyboard/menu fixes (bbhost v0.2.24):
Adapted from https://github.com/droogie/bbhost at
b0098e04b889e2e70b4af84be1ce809d7af3ff95 (GPL-3.0-or-later).
Sources include src/decomp/gx/job_barrier.cpp and its differential test,
src/host/bindings.cpp, and src/engine/menu_pointer.cpp. Cachyborne uses
its own runtime, byte-checked hooks and Vulkan recording pipeline.

Game-time clock, replay/sync and native frame-clock consumers:
Adapted from the same bbhost v0.2.24 revision, engine/frame_clock.h,
decomp/chr/chr_sync.cpp, decomp/chr/replay_manipulator.cpp,
decomp/physics/ragdoll_drive.cpp, decomp/yebis/ppfx_setters.cpp and their
retail differential test fixtures (GPL-3.0-or-later). Cachyborne uses its
own packed clock publication and byte-checked guest trampolines.
Frame-driven MagicOrchestra sound-thread wake: adapted from the same revision,
src/engine/sound_wake.{h,cpp} (GPL-3.0-or-later).
Wind timeline and force at unlocked frame rates: adapted from the same revision,
src/engine/wind_pace.h and frame_rate.cpp (GPL-3.0-or-later).

Optional last-input priority for opposing movement keys: inspired by
Mrsuss60/bloodborne_pc_windows_port commit
8ea9aa3744c6e59ada2ed041c65e524c0a2837bb, src/runtime_pad.c (GPL-2.0-or-later).
Cachyborne keeps BBHOST's sprint momentum and independent camera smoothing.

Hunter's Dream mirror world-layout generator: adapted from bbhost v0.2.24,
src/engine/dream_mirror_layout.{h,cpp} (GPL-3.0-or-later), commit
b0098e04b889e2e70b4af84be1ce809d7af3ff95. No game bytes are included.
Menu-step observation and reference ownership: adapted from the same revision,
src/engine/menu_steps.{h,cpp} (GPL-3.0-or-later), with checked atomic reference
operations and a shared frame-task observer for host features.
Experimental appearance-preview window controller: adapted from the same revision,
src/engine/change_appearance.cpp (GPL-3.0-or-later). Cachyborne holds the list's
reference before guest window allocation and closes the preview on world teardown.

Reserved GCN descriptor encodings:
Adapted from bloodborne-native/bloodborne-runtime commit
e207326050a31ccd9e09d5d56bd1cc275816cbd8 (GPL-2.0-or-later),
https://github.com/bloodborne-native/bloodborne-runtime . Cachyborne also
skips invalid vertex formats in both regular and prepared input paths.

Deferred recording data lifetime: informed by the chunk-overflow fix in
Mrsuss60/bloodborne_pc_windows_port commit
3e600386439130a981259b84076a21a7bb31c3f6 (GPL-2.0-or-later).
Cachyborne uses its own chunk-owned aligned overflow and batch boundaries;
pipeline serialization and malformed-packet suppression are not imported.

Resident shader-specialization ownership and profile publication before recipe
import: informed by Mrsuss60/bloodborne_pc_windows_port commits
ce83b806b9975185b801355d73fb5ea50aa5b314 and
432d2ddbf1547f6f24e87d27295a168355242a1b (GPL-2.0-or-later).
Cachyborne rebases specialization ownership at Program insertion and uses its
own sequence-based BlobStore visibility barrier with write-failure reporting;
foreign metadata layouts and cache-version migrations are not imported.

Optional FMOD project language-count initialization: adapted from BBHOST PR #104,
https://github.com/droogie/bbhost/pull/104 (GPL-3.0-or-later).
Cachyborne observes the byte-checked constructor entry and preserves the entire
retail constructor; its regression executes that constructor from a local dump.

Bounded GX upload-block reclaim and discard-copy recovery:
Adapted from droogie/bbhost commit 7dbe6f60f33fff45ea1bcbf6c6e61a6b35466e13,
src/decomp/gx/block_reclaim.cpp and rename_wait.cpp (GPL-3.0-or-later).
Cachyborne retries the exact failed copy allocation inside the retail function;
its Vulkan bridge preserves producer ownership and waits for CPU labels too.

Save before exit to desktop:
Adapted from ayozetr/bloodborne_linux commit
1d0bbec9785843eca8661f481f3a7f47de126829 (GPL-2.0-or-later),
gpu/shim/bbport_game_menu.cpp and src/runtime_services.c/runtime_savedata.c.
Cachyborne arms only from the original affirmative callback, follows retail
functor clones across threads, and gates closure on title plus all save unmounts.

Offline named parameter inspection:
scripts/param_tables.py adapts tools/bbparam.py and src/engine/paramdef.cpp
from droogie/bbhost revision bdc5cdf8be5f37188da9c2368e92be444fdc04cb
(https://github.com/droogie/bbhost, GPL-3.0-or-later). Cachyborne adds bounded
archive, definition and row validation and reuses its DCX decoder. This tool
does not include the upstream live table modification or plugin service.

Read-only loaded parameter repository access:
gpu/games/bloodborne/params.{h,cpp} adapts src/engine/params.cpp from the same
BBHOST bdc5cdf8be5f37188da9c2368e92be444fdc04cb revision. Cachyborne uses a
bounded injectable reader and resolves current resources on demand, without
adding default frame polling, cached guest pointers or a mutation service.

Online/offline title choice:
Adapted from bloodborne-native/bloodborne-runtime commit
cf57dc0e0ebdb1562fa43ad002d0202a1d1fc480 (GPL-2.0-or-later), scripts/patches.py.
Cachyborne also projects the online choice into its native launcher settings;
an explicit extra-environment override remains available.

Optional adaptive frame limiter:
gpu/shim/bbport_limiter.{h,cpp} adapts the sleep-margin policy from
droogie/bbhost revision bdc5cdf8be5f37188da9c2368e92be444fdc04cb,
src/engine/frame_rate.cpp (GPL-3.0-or-later). Cachyborne retains the retail
